{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1291845-weapons-in-aeon","id":1291845,"title":"Weapons in Aeon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-25T08:25:40-08:00","id":1291845,"title":"Weapons in Aeon","content":"I'm having trouble figuring out how to design new weapons in Aeon. Specifically I'm trying to reverse engineer the enhancer gauntlet down to it's costs so I can turn it into something a biotech scientist might own (either more like the electro gauntlet, or just more focused on electromanipulation enhancement), but in general I want to understand how to make weapons.<br /> <br /> Even in the core book it seems confusing. It seems like a pistol is a wealth 3 item and the assault rifle is wealth 5. That seems high.<br /> <br /> The enhancer gauntlet seems to be a cost 8 item not a cost 3 item.<br /> <br /> Beam (1)<br /> Destructive (2)<br /> Formatted 2 (2)<br /> Psi Gauntlet (0)<br /> Ranged (1)<br /> Super-Science 1 (1)<br /> (It also appears to have Quality 2 to give it it's one extra enhancement bonus over the formatting 2 inherent bonus even though it's not listed)<br /> <br /> It gets 1 tag free and +1 enhancement free according to the core book's section on building weapons. It still has 8 points worth of tags beyond the free one. How does it get to be cost 3?<br /> <br /> <br /> The electrolaser gauntlet doesn't seem to add up either.<br /> <br /> Electrical (1)<br /> Formatted 1 (1)<br /> Optionally Non-Lethal 3 (3)<br /> Psi Gauntlet (0)<br /> Ranged (1)<br /> Super Science (1)<br /> <br /> It says cost 3 but that adds up to 6 for me. Where does it get enhancement 3 from? I see 2 from its Optionally Non-Lethal 3, but it only has Formatted 1 so it doesn't get an inherent +1 enhancement from that. I'm assuming that super science tag pays for being able to spend a psi point to modify the attack.<br /> <br /> Just 2 examples of how none of the psi gauntlets seem to add up. I can't figure out what I a missing. Same issue with a lot of the armors.<br /> <br /> Clearly there's a variable that I am missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:35:03-08:00","id":1291958,"title":"","content":"The total of tags an weapon have is equal to tags + 1 on TC (page 121), but on Aeon (page 278, on the entrance tags) it\u2019s 4+ tags. So by your counts it\u2019s cost should be 5 (what I agree). I would say the enhancement is for the formatted, as it cannot be used unformatted, in this case the quality 2 is dropped and the count is correct.<br /> <br /> For the electrolaser the counting works if you reduce the enhancement to 2 (no quality 2 tag)<br /> <br /> What really annoys me about it all is the Super Science tag that have the worst description possible. Not even a hint on how it works. As I reversed I would say a bonus on psi (to set the effects) is worth 1 tag, an 1 dot power (in the case Tow) worth a 1 poin, a tag 2 that require Psi use worth 1 and a situational +2 en worth a 1. They could have put some better guidelines for that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T17:15:50-08:00","id":1292019,"title":"","content":"Ah thank you. I did not see that Aeon weapons get more free tags. The electrolaser works for the same thing you pointed out for the enhancer. It can only be used formatted so always count that bonus, and optional non-lethal 2 makes the basic attack enhancement 2.<br /> <br /> For super science you take that rank back to the core super science chapter. It fits more evenly for the enhancer gauntlet as some sort of +1 to one thing. The super science bonus for the electro gauntlet doesn't map directly to that chart in the core but it's a fairly simple bonus so calling it rank 1 super science is a fair cost.<br /> <br /> Now I should be able to work up a cost for some sort of psi enhancing electromanipulation gauntlet. I guess it would effectively just be an IAD though. The IAD already adds up to a super science 3 device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}